  "_id": "tg-fruit",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "fruit tree yielding fruit after his kind, Gen. 1:11 (Moses 2:11; Abr. 4:11). of the fruit of the tree … Ye shall not eat, Gen. 3:3. Cain brought of the fruit of the ground, Gen. 4:3 (Moses 5:19). he will also bless the fruit of thy womb, Deut. 7:13 (Luke 1:42). thou shalt take of the first of all the fruit, Deut. 26:2. Blessed shall be the fruit of thy body, Deut. 28:4. precious fruits brought forth by the sun, Deut. 33:14. bringeth forth his fruit in his season, Ps. 1:3. They shall still bring forth fruit in old age, Ps. 92:14. fruit of the womb is his reward, Ps. 127:3. fruit of thy body will I set upon thy throne, Ps. 132:11 (Acts 2:30). they eat of the fruit of their own way, Prov. 1:31. My fruit is better than gold, Prov. 8:19. fruit of the righteous is a tree of life, Prov. 11:30. fruit of the earth shall be excellent, Isa. 4:2 (2 Ne. 14:2). fill the face of the world with fruit, Isa. 27:6. I create the fruit of the lips, Isa. 57:19. bring evil upon this people, even the fruit of their thoughts, Jer. 6:19. he bringeth forth fruit unto himself, Hosea 10:1. neither shall fruit be in the vines, Hab. 3:17. earth is stayed from her fruit, Hag. 1:10.",
